    <tags>trackhop music playlist sync spotify youtube-music tidal navidrome subsonic jellyfin plex foss</tags>
    <summary>Keeps playlists in sync between music services (beta)</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[Trackhop Desktop is the sync engine of the Trackhop Android app as a program for your computer, with its own Java runtime: nothing else to install.

It keeps playlists in sync between Spotify, YouTube, TIDAL, Navidrome and other Subsonic servers, Jellyfin, Plex, Last.fm, ListenBrainz, SoundCloud links and CSV files, on a schedule, with an icon next to the clock. Its pages open in its own window and at `http://127.0.0.1:8642`, reachable only from this computer.

**Beta:** it works for everyday use, but pages and settings can still change between releases.

## Notes

- The installer is per user: Trackhop is installed into `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Trackhop` of the account that runs `choco install` (normally yours, elevated). Installing from another administrator account or as SYSTEM installs it for that account instead.
- The data (syncs, sign-ins, log) is kept in `%APPDATA%\Trackhop` and stays when the package is uninstalled.
- Its window uses Microsoft Edge WebView2, part of Windows 10 and 11; without it the pages open in the browser.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/xlollx/Trackhop/releases/tag/server-v0.5.1</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
